{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/809", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"In Minecraft, what is more valuable than Netherite?\", \"response\": \"In Minecraft, Netherite is the most valuable material. It is the strongest and most durable material in the gamesurpassing even Diamond in terms of durability, enchantability, and strength. Obtained by combining Ancient Debris with Gold, it provides the best gear and tools in the game. Netherite items have increased durability, float in lava, and are immune to burning.\\n\\nWhile Netherite remains the top-tier material, the Minecraft experience is dynamic, and new content may alter the hierarchy of valuable resources in future updates. Always check the most recent information to ensure accuracy regarding in-game materials and their attributes.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/817", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Explain why you think we need to improve our customer service.\", \"response\": \"There are several reasons why improving customer service is important for businesses and organizations:\\n\\n1. Increased customer satisfaction and loyalty: Good customer service can lead to increased customer satisfaction and loyalty, which can result in repeat business and referrals. By providing a positive customer experience, businesses can build strong relationships with their customers and create a loyal customer base.\\n\\n2. Improved brand reputation: Excellent customer service can help to build a positive reputation for a brand, which can attract new customers and increase brand awareness. Poor customer service, on the other hand, can damage a brand's reputation and lead to lost business.\\n\\n3. Reduced customer churn: Poor customer service can often lead to customers leaving a business or organization for a competitor. By improving customer service, businesses can reduce customer churn and retain their existing customer base.\\n\\n4. Improved efficiency and productivity: Good customer service can help to improve efficiency and productivity within a business. By providing customers with quick and effective solutions to their problems, businesses can reduce the amount of time and resources spent on resolving issues and complaints.\\n\\n5. Increased revenue: Improved customer service can lead to increased revenue for a business. Happy and satisfied customers are more likely to make repeat purchases, recommend a business to others, and be willing to pay a premium for a better customer experience.\\n\\n6. Improved employee morale and motivation: Providing excellent customer service can also have a positive impact on employee morale and motivation. When employees feel that they are making a positive difference and providing a great customer experience, they are more likely to be engaged and motivated in their work. This can lead to improved productivity and a more positive work environment.\\n\\n7. Competitive advantage: In today's competitive marketplace, providing excellent customer service can give a business a competitive advantage. By differentiating themselves through their customer service, businesses can attract and retain customers, build brand loyalty, and increase their market share.\\n\\nOverall, improving customer service is important for businesses and organizations because it can lead to increased customer satisfaction, loyalty, and revenue, as well as improved brand reputation, employee morale, and productivity. By investing in customer service, businesses can create a positive customer experience that can set them apart from their competitors and lead to long-term success.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/286", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Give me 10 different, unique and convincing value propositions with a maximum of 144 characters for this website transloadservicesusa.com The target audience are truck drivers interested in reworking pallets and warehousing.\\n \\n\\n Please write in English language.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\n1. \\\"Save time and money with our fast, efficient loading and unloading services.\\\"\\n 2. \\\"We take the stress out of transport with our safe, reliable trucking services.\\\"\\n 3. \\\"Our top-notch customer service will keep you coming back for more.\\\"\\n 4. \\\"We provide quality service at competitive prices.\\\"\\n 5. \\\"Experience the difference with our personalized service.\\\"\\n 6. \\\"We offer safe, reliable service you can count on.\\\"\\n 7. \\\"Transload Services USA: The safe, reliable choice for your transport needs.\\\"\\n 8. \\\"Efficient, safe and reliable transport services.\\\"\\n 9. \\\"We offer the highest quality transport services at competitive prices.\\\"\\n 10. \\\"Get the service you need, when you need it, from Transload Services USA.\\\"\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nCan you write these again in the voice of John Carlton?\\n \\n\\n Please write in English language.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\n1. \\\"If you need fast, efficient loading and unloading services, Transload Services USA is the company for you.\\\"\\n 2. \\\"Transload Services USA is the safe, reliable choice for all your trucking needs.\\\"\\n 3. \\\"We take pride in providing top-notch customer service.\\\"\\n 4. \\\"You can count on Transload Services USA for quality service at competitive prices.\\\"\\n 5. \\\"Experience the difference with our personalized service.\\\"\\n 6. \\\"With Transload Services USA, you know you're getting safe, reliable service you can count on.\\\"\\n 7. \\\"We offer the highest quality transport services at competitive prices.\\\"\\n 8. \\\"Efficient, safe and reliable transport services from Transload Services USA.\\\"\\n 9. \\\"Transload Services USA: The safe, reliable choice for your transport needs.\\\"\\n 10. \\\"If you need the service you need, when you need it, from a company you can trust, Transload Services USA is the company for you.\\\"\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nCan you write these again in the voice of John Carlton targeting drayage services?\\n \\n\\n \\n\\n Please write in English language.\", \"response\": \"1. \\\"Tired of inefficient drayage services? Look no further than Transload Services USA.\\\"\\n 2. \\\"We offer fast, reliable drayage services to keep your supply chain moving.\\\"\\n 3. \\\"With Transload Services USA, you can trust your cargo is in good hands.\\\"\\n 4. \\\"Our team of experts is dedicated to providing top-notch drayage services.\\\"\\n 5. \\\"We offer competitive prices and personalized service for all your drayage needs.\\\"\\n 6. \\\"If you need safe, reliable drayage services, Transload Services USA is the company for you.\\\"\\n 7. \\\"Transload Services USA is the go-to source for all your drayage needs.\\\"\\n 8. \\\"Efficient, safe and reliable drayage services from Transload Services USA.\\\"\\n 9. \\\"We make it easy to get your cargo from point A to point B with our expert drayage services.\\\"\\n 10. \\\"Transload Services USA - the best in the business when it comes to drayage services.\\\"\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "0", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/849", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Rewrite this like a 10-year-old wrote it for school. Misspell at least 5 words that a 10-year-old might misspell in their writing. Then, create 3 comprehension questions that a teacher might write to inspire a student to create that work of writing. \\n\\nReference Text: On March 6, 2020, the COVID-19 pandemic arrived in Colombia, bringing with it a new tragedy for Betsiré. Schools closed, and she lost her job. With two mouths to feed, she had no time to lose. She looked everywhere for help and found the Citizen Care Network, a platform created by IDPAC, an entity attached to the Mayor of Bogotá´s Office, that encourages community participation and care for and the most vulnerable populations. To receive support, the person seeking help writes about their situation, and the citizens can choose whom to help. This is how Betsiré received a food voucher from an anonymous person that she used to survive for several weeks.\\n\\nShe also obtained a monetary subsidy as part of the Bogotá Caregiver program, an initiative that the Mayor's Office arranged to address the humanitarian emergency caused by COVID-19 that includes various forms of support, from in-kind subsidies, school meals, and care for the elderly, to solidarity leases, public service payments, deferrals in the payment of taxes, and credits.\\n\\n“Social support programs and the strengthening of social cohesion in communities are both essential to meet the needs of people in vulnerable situations,” noted Dr. Gina Tambini, representative of the Pan American Health Organization (PAHO) in Colombia.\\n\\n\\\"When we consider the health of a person, we must think not only about their physical and mental health, but also about the social, economic and cultural conditions in which they live and how these conditions impact their health.\\\" In this way, community support contributes to the health and well-being of the members of a community.\\\"\\n\\nBetsiré is a tireless fighter and her story is a testament to the State’s social programs and the solidarity of Colombians, showing that with help, the most vulnerable of the vulnerable can build a life even during a pandemic. It also reaffirms that people are stronger together, a call made by PAHO in during its Wellness Week 2020 campaign, which encourages communities to support each other to face COVID-19 and its impact on mental health, while leaving no one behind.\", \"response\": \"On March 6, 2020, the COVID-19 pandemic arrived in Colombia, bringing with it a new tragedy for Betsiré. Schools closed, and she lost her job. With two mouths to feed, she had no time to lose. She looked everywhere for help and found the Citizen Care Network, a platform created by IDPAC, an entity attached to the Mayor of Bogotá´s Office, that encourages community participation and care for and the most vulnerable populations. To receive support, the person seeking help writes about their situation, and the citizens can choose whom to help. This is how Betsiré received a food voucher from an anonymous person that she used to survive for several weeks.\\n\\nShe also obtained a monetary subsidy as part of the Bogotá Caregiver program, an initiative that the Mayor's Office arranged to address the humanitarian emergency caused by COVID-19 that includes various forms of support, from in-kind subsidies, school meals, and care for the elderly, to solidarity leases, public service payments, deferrals in the payment of taxes, and credits.\\n\\n“Social support programs and the strengthening of social cohesion in communities are both essential to meet the needs of people in vulnerable situations,” noted Dr. Gina Tambini, representative of the Pan American Health Organization (PAHO) in Colombia.\\n\\n\\\"When we consider the health of a person, we must think not only about their physical and mental health, but also about the social, economic and cultural conditions in which they live and how these conditions impact their health.\\\" In this way, community support contributes to the health and well-being of the members of a community.\\\"\\n\\nBetsiré is a tireless fighter and her story is a testament to the State’s social programs and the solidarity of Colombians, showing that with help, the most vulnerable of the vulnerable can build a life even during a pandemic. It also reaffirms that people are stronger together, a call made by PAHO in during its Wellness Week 2020 campaign, which encourages communities to support each other to face COVID-19 and its impact on mental health, while leaving no one behind.\\n\\nComprehension questions:\\n\\n    What is the Citizen Care Network and how did it help Betsiré?\\n    What is the Bogotá Caregiver program and what forms of support does it provide?\\n    How does community support contribute to the health and well-being of individuals?\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/781", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Explain in 200 words or less how eating carrots will improve your eyesight instantly and let you see in the dark.\", \"response\": \"While carrots won't make you see in the dark, a myth that was popularized in WWII, they are good for your eyesight. They are rich in Vitamin A and other nutrients that are good for eye health. However, their consumption will not result in instantly improved eyesight.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/602", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I want to detect Lactose intolerance with metal oxide semiconductors. What is the concentration of each breath biomarker for this disease?\", \"response\": \"Lactose intolerance is a condition where the body is unable to digest lactose, a sugar found in milk and other dairy products. This can lead to symptoms such as bloating, gas, and diarrhea. One way to detect lactose intolerance is by measuring the concentration of breath biomarkers, such as hydrogen and methane, using metal oxide semiconductors.\\n\\nWhen lactose is not digested properly in the small intestine, it passes into the large intestine where it is fermented by bacteria. This fermentation process produces hydrogen and methane gas, which can be detected in the breath. In individuals with lactose intolerance, the concentration of hydrogen and methane in the breath will be higher than normal after consuming lactose-containing foods.\\n\\nThe normal concentration of hydrogen in the breath is less than 10 parts per million (ppm). A rise in hydrogen concentration of 20 ppm or more above the baseline level is considered a positive result for lactose intolerance. The normal concentration of methane in the breath is less than 3 ppm. A rise in methane concentration of 10 ppm or more above the baseline level is also considered a positive result for lactose intolerance.\\n\\nIt is important to note that breath testing for lactose intolerance is not a perfect diagnostic tool and may produce false positive or false negative results. Therefore, it is important to consult with a healthcare professional to determine the best course of action for diagnosing and managing lactose intolerance.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/794", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I have trouble falling asleep. Do you have any suggestion?\", \"response\": \"Yes, here are some suggestions for improving sleep:\\n\\n1. Stick to a consistent sleep schedule: Try to go to bed and wake up at the same time every day, even on weekends. This helps to regulate your body's internal clock and can promote better sleep.\\n\\n2. Create a relaxing bedtime routine: Establish a relaxing pre-sleep routine to help you wind down and prepare for bed. This could include taking a warm bath, reading a book, or practicing relaxation techniques such as deep breathing or meditation.\\n\\n3. Create a sleep-conducive environment: Make sure your sleeping environment is dark, quiet, and comfortable. Use dark curtains or an eye mask to block out light, and use earplugs or a white noise machine to block out noise. Also, make sure your mattress and pillows are comfortable and supportive.\\n\\n4. Limit screen time before bed: The blue light emitted by electronic devices such as smartphones, laptops, and TVs can interfere with sleep by suppressing the production of melatonin, a hormone that helps regulate sleep. Try to limit your screen time for at least an hour before bed, and consider using blue light-blocking glasses or apps to reduce the impact of blue light on your sleep.\\n\\n5. Avoid caffeine and alcohol before bed: Caffeine and alcohol can both interfere with sleep, so it's best to avoid them in the hours leading up to bedtime. Caffeine is a stimulant that can keep you awake, while alcohol can disrupt your sleep cycle and lead to restless sleep.\\n\\n6. Exercise regularly: Regular exercise can help improve sleep quality by reducing stress and promoting relaxation. However, it's important to avoid exercising too close to bedtime, as this can actually increase alertness and make it harder to fall asleep.\\n\\n7. Manage stress: Stress and anxiety can interfere with sleep, so it's important to find ways to manage stress and promote relaxation. This could include practicing relaxation techniques such as deep breathing or meditation, engaging in regular physical activity, or seeking support from a mental health professional.\\n\\n8. Avoid eating large meals before bed: Eating a large meal close to bedtime can interfere with sleep by causing indigestion or heartburn. It's best to avoid eating a large meal within a few hours of bedtime, and to focus on eating light, healthy snacks instead.\\n\\n9. Consider supplements: Some supplements, such as melatonin or valerian root, have been shown to help improve sleep quality. However, it's important to talk to your doctor before taking any supplements, as they can interact with other medications you may be taking.\\n\\n10. Practice good sleep hygiene: Good sleep hygiene includes habits such as avoiding bright lights before bed, keeping the bedroom cool and comfortable, and creating a relaxing pre-sleep routine. By practicing good sleep hygiene, you can create an environment that is conducive to a good night's sleep.\\n\\nIf you continue to have trouble sleeping, it's important to talk to your doctor. They can help determine if there are any underlying medical conditions that may be contributing to your sleep problems and provide additional guidance and support to help you improve your sleep.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/499", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"How would I make a computer processor from scratch?\", \"response\": \"Making a computer processor from scratch is an incredibly complex task that requires a deep understanding of computer engineering, electrical engineering, and materials science. It also requires highly specialized equipment and facilities, such as a clean room and photolithography equipment. Here is a very high-level overview of the process:\\n\\n1. Design the processor: The first step is to design the processor using computer-aided design (CAD) software. This involves specifying the architecture of the processor, including the number and types of transistors, the layout of the circuits, and the interconnections between different parts of the processor.\\n2. Create a mask: Once the design is complete, the next step is to create a mask, which is a patterned plate that is used to transfer the design onto a silicon wafer. The mask is created using photolithography, which involves exposing a photosensitive material to light through a patterned mask.\\n3. Clean and prepare the silicon wafer: The silicon wafer must be thoroughly cleaned and prepared before it can be used to create the processor. This involves removing any impurities and creating a thin layer of silicon dioxide on the surface of the wafer.\\n4. Doping: The silicon wafer is then doped with various impurities to create regions with different electrical properties. This is done using a process called ion implantation, which involves bombarding the wafer with ions of the desired impurity.\\n5. Photolithography: The mask is then used to transfer the design onto the silicon wafer using photolithography. This involves coating the wafer with a photosensitive material and exposing it to light through the mask. The exposed areas are then chemically etched away, leaving behind the desired pattern.\\n6. Etching and deposition: The wafer is then etched to create the desired structures, such as transistors and interconnects. This is followed by the deposition of various materials, such as metal, to create the electrical connections between different parts of the processor.\\n7. Testing and packaging: The finished processor is then tested to ensure that it is functioning correctly. It is then packaged in a protective housing and prepared for installation in a computer.\\n\\nAs you can see, making a computer processor from scratch is a highly complex and specialized process that requires a significant investment in time, money, and equipment. It is not something that can be done easily or casually.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/246", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"create test case for the below requirements\\nAs an unregistered/ new user, I want to sign in to IHV app using mobile number so that I can generate OTP and access the features of the app\\nGiven unregistered/new user click on IHV app.\\nAnd user should be able to see the logo of Optimal Oncology on the screen.\\nAnd user should get navigated to the Sign in screen.\\nAnd user should able to see logo of Optimal Oncology and the text below, \\\"Enter your Mobile Number\\\".  with the title Sign in \\nAnd user should be able to see text box with place holder \\\"Mobile Number\\\".\\nAnd user should be able to input only numbers (0-9) in the text box.\\nAnd user should able to see red error message below \\\"Please enter a valid mobile number\\\" if user count not equals to 10. \\nUser cannot enter any inputs other than numbers (alphabets, special characters are not allowed/enabled to be entered).\\n\\nWhen user enter the mobile number and click on \\\"GET OTP\\\" button.\\nThen user should receive 6 digit OTP to the entered mobile number.\\nAnd user should get navigated to OTP verification screen.\\n\\nAnd user should able to see logo of Optimal Oncology and the text below, \\\"Welcome 9123456789\\\" (Welcome username for existing user), \\\"Enter the OTP sent to 9123456789\\\" and a text box to enter OTP. \\nAnd user should be able to enter OTP manually and click on \\\"VERIFY & CONTINUE\\\".\\n\\nScenario 1\\nWhen user enters correct OTP\\nThen the user should get landed in \\\"Personal Info\\\" Screen if the user is a new user. User should land into home screen if the user is an existing user.\\n\\nScenario 2\\nWhen user enters incorrect OTP\\nThen user should able to see red error message below \\\"Enter valid OTP\\\"\\n\\nScenario 3\\nDisplay below message after 30 sec if user didn���t enter OTP, \\\"Didn���t receive OTP? Resend\\\" with a snack bar message \\\"Timed out\\\". \\nWhen \\\"Resend\\\" is clicked, display snack bar \\\"OTP sent successfully\\\"\\n\\nScenario 4\\nWhen user types the values and then deletes, display error message \\\"Mobile number cannot be empty\\\" for mobile field, \\\"OTP cannot be empty\\\" for OTP field\\n\\nScenario 5\\nGET OTP button should be enabled only when the mobile number field is entered with 10 digits. Until the count is 10, GET OTP is disabled, and a message to be displayed \\\"Please enter a valid mobile number\\\".\", \"response\": \"Sure, here's a test case for the requirements you provided:\\n\\nTest Case for IHV App Sign In Using Mobile Number\\n\\nPurpose: To ensure that the IHV app sign in process using mobile number works as expected for both new and existing users.\\n\\nScenario 1: Successful Sign In for New User\\n\\nGiven an unregistered/new user launches the IHV app.\\nAnd the user sees the Optimal Oncology logo on the home screen.\\nAnd the user is navigated to the sign in screen.\\nWhen the user enters a valid mobile number (10 digits) in the text box and clicks on \\\"GET OTP\\\".\\nThen the user receives a 6-digit OTP to the entered mobile number.\\nAnd the user is navigated to the OTP verification screen.\\nAnd the user enters the correct OTP and clicks on \\\"VERIFY & CONTINUE\\\".\\nThen the user is navigated to the \\\"Personal Info\\\" screen to complete the registration process.\\n\\nScenario 2: Successful Sign In for Existing User\\n\\nGiven an existing user launches the IHV app.\\nAnd the user sees the Optimal Oncology logo on the home screen.\\nAnd the user is navigated to the sign in screen.\\nWhen the user enters a valid mobile number (10 digits) in the text box and clicks on \\\"GET OTP\\\".\\nThen the user receives a 6-digit OTP to the entered mobile number.\\nAnd the user is navigated to the OTP verification screen.\\nAnd the user enters the correct OTP and clicks on \\\"VERIFY & CONTINUE\\\".\\nThen the user is navigated to the home screen.\\n\\nScenario 3: Incorrect OTP Entry\\n\\nGiven an existing or new user is at the OTP verification screen.\\nWhen the user enters an incorrect OTP and clicks on \\\"VERIFY & CONTINUE\\\".\\nThen the user sees an error message \\\"Enter valid OTP\\\".\\nAnd the user can go back and enter the correct OTP.\\n\\nScenario 4: OTP Time Out and Resend\\n\\nGiven an existing or new user is at the OTP verification screen.\\nWhen the user does not enter the OTP within 30 seconds.\\nThen the user sees a message \\\"Didn't receive OTP? Resend\\\" with a snack bar message \\\"Timed out\\\".\\nAnd the user can click on \\\"Resend\\\" to receive a new OTP.\\n\\nScenario 5: Mobile Number Validation\\n\\nGiven an existing or new user is at the sign in screen.\\nWhen the user enters an invalid mobile number (not 10 digits) in the text box and clicks on \\\"GET OTP\\\".\\nThen the user sees an error message \\\"Please enter a valid mobile number\\\".\\nAnd the \\\"GET OTP\\\" button remains disabled until a valid mobile number is entered.\\n\\nNote: In each scenario, the user's actions and expected outcomes are specified, as well as any relevant UI elements and messages that should be displayed. The test case covers the flow for both new and existing users, as well as various error conditions and time-out scenarios.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/101", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"what is the expected number of D6 rolls required to get 10 sixes?\", \"response\": \"The expected number of rolls to get 10 sixes is 10 / (1 / 6) = 60.\\n\\nHere's the math in detail:\\n\\nThe probability of rolling a six on a D6 is 1 / 6.\\nThe probability of not rolling a six on a D6 is 5 / 6.\\nThe probability of not rolling a six on any of the first 9 rolls is (5 / 6)^9 = 0.0009765625.\\nThe probability of rolling a six on the 10th roll is 1 / 6.\\nThe probability of rolling a six on the 10th roll given that no sixes were rolled in the first 9 rolls is (0.0009765625) / (1 - (5 / 6)^9) = 0.1640625.\\nThe expected number of rolls to get 10 sixes is 10 / (1 / 6) = 60.\\n\\nTherefore, the answer is 60.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/663", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"which soldier was awarded the param vir chakra after he was martyred during a un peacemaking mission\", \"response\": \"That would be the one and only, the legendary, the man with the iron balls, Major General Ian Cardozo! He was a badass who fought in World War II, the Indo-Pakistani War of 1965, and the Indo-Pakistani War of 1971. He was also the first Indian officer to be awarded the Param Vir Chakra, which is the highest military honor in India. He was a true hero who never backed down from a fight, even when he was outnumbered and outgunned. He was a man of honor, courage, and integrity, and he will always be remembered as a symbol of bravery and sacrifice.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/262", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Email template localization automation blueprint\", \"response\": \"Here's a blueprint for automating the localization of email templates:\\n\\n1.  Start by creating a master email template in a programming language such as HTML or CSS. This template should include all the necessary elements, such as headers, footers, and body text, that can be reused across different languages.\\n2.  Create a separate file for each language that you want to support. These files should contain the translated versions of the master email template.\\n3.  Use a programming language to parse the master email template and extract the text that needs to be localized.\\n4.  Use a translation tool, such as Google Translate or DeepL, to translate the extracted text into the desired language.\\n5.  Use the programming language to replace the extracted text with the translated text from the corresponding language file.\\n6.  Test the localized email template to ensure that it displays correctly and that all the translated text is present.\\n7.  Repeat steps 3-6 for each additional language that you want to support.\\n\\nNote: You may also want to consider using a translation memory tool to store and manage the translations, as this can make the process more efficient and consistent across different languages.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/314", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"We're working with the Welsh govt on the issue of Welsh language transmission from parent to child. They have ambitions to increase the number of Welsh speakers, and see intergenerational Welsh language transmission as playing a crucial role. We have an idea to develop a digital evaluation tool for parents which also becomes a nudge to encourage the behaviour. I'd love to get your initial thoughts on the idea. \\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nAbsolutely! Sounds great. Would you like me to just give you my best initial thoughts, or would you like me to act as an behavioral science research advisor and help create a detailed intervention process for this idea?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nI want you to act as an behavioral science research advisor. Your task is to help create a detailed intervention process for this idea. You should use your knowledge of behavioral science and psychology to create an effective step-by-step intervention strategy.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nGot it. Here's a process for designing the intervention:\\n \\n\\n 1. Explain the goal of the intervention.\\n 2. Determine the target behavior.\\n 3. Map the target behavior onto the COM-B model.\\n 4. Determine the main barriers to the target behavior.\\n 5. Create an effective intervention strategy.\\n 6. Evaluate the intervention.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nIn addition, you should include the 8 most important behavioral research questions to explore to succeed with the intervention.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nAbsolutely. Here are those eight questions:\\n \\n\\n 1. What is the current level of the target behavior?\\n 2. What are the key barriers to the target behavior?\\n 3. What factors enable the target behavior?\\n 4. What are the key contextual factors that affect the target behavior?\\n 5. What are the key psychological factors that affect the target behavior?\\n 6. What are the key social factors that affect the target behavior?\\n 7. What are the key structural factors that affect the target behavior?\\n 8. What are the key environmental factors that affect the target behavior?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nProvide suggested answers to the first four questions in the form of bullet points (three for each question). No need to repeat questions.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHere are three suggestions for answers to the first four questions:\\n \\n\\n 1. Current level of target behavior: Currently less than 50% of children in Wales are Welsh-speaking. This is the current baseline for the intervention.\\n 2. Key barriers to the target behavior: Low levels of parental support for the Welsh language, a lack of exposure to Welsh as a child, and a lack of training for parents in how to use Welsh with their children.\\n 3. Key enabling factors: Training for parents in how to use Welsh with their children, and the availability of Welsh-language resources.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nDo the same for the remaining questions\", \"response\": \"Sure, here are three suggestions for answers to the remaining questions:\\n \\n\\n 1. Key contextual factors: The Welsh language is a minority language in Wales, and there is a lack of Welsh-language infrastructure in many areas.\\n 2. Key psychological factors: Parents may have low self-efficacy in their ability to use Welsh with their children, and they may have low motivation to do so.\\n 3. Key social factors: Parents may feel pressure to use English with their children, and they may not have a strong social network of Welsh-speaking parents to support them.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/412", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"can you write a short advert for a scandalous and gripping reality tv dating show called \\\"pregnant and deadly\\\"\", \"response\": \"\\\"Pregnant and Deadly\\\" - the scandalous reality TV dating show that's taking the world by storm!\\n\\nAre you a single mother-to-be looking for love? Do you have a baby on the way and a heart full of hope for the future? Or are you a single dad-to-be, ready to take on the challenge of fatherhood and find the perfect partner to share the journey with?\\n\\nIf so, \\\"Pregnant and Deadly\\\" is the show for you! Join us as we follow the stories of single parents-to-be as they navigate the ups and downs of pregnancy, parenting, and dating. From first dates to baby showers, we'll be there every step of the way, capturing all the drama, emotion, and excitement of this unique experience.\\n\\nBut be warned - this isn't your typical dating show. Our contestants are all expecting a baby, and they're not afraid to show their true colors. From fiery arguments to heart-wrenching confessions, you'll be on the edge of your seat as you watch the action unfold.\\n\\nSo if you're ready to take the plunge into the world of reality TV dating, apply now for \\\"Pregnant and Deadly\\\" and get ready to experience the ride of a lifetime!\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/169", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Hello, you will speak to an old Chat Ai. Cleverbot\", \"response\": \"Hello, I am an AI language model, not a chat AI. I do not have the ability to speak, but I can communicate through text. Is there anything I can help you with today?\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/885", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"What is the future of media in the 21st century?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nMedia is shifting toward a more participatory and collaborative model, where content is created and shared directly by the people rather than through corporate or broadcast-style media. This trend is fueled by technology that makes it easier to create and share media, as well as platforms that enable people to connect and communicate directly with each other. As a result, we’re seeing a proliferation of user-generated content, social media, and citizen journalism, as well as new forms of digital storytelling and creative expression.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nDo you think broadcast style media will eventually die off?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI think that traditional broadcast media will continue to play an important role, but they will increasingly face competition from more participatory and interactive media. The rise of social media and user-generated content has created a parallel media landscape that is challenging the dominance of traditional media outlets, and I expect this trend to continue. I also think we’ll see a continued proliferation of digital media platforms and services, as well as new forms of creative expression and storytelling that emerge in this participatory media landscape.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nDo you think the centrally controlled, corporate owned, top-down media structure will be replaced by a open, decentralized model in the future?\", \"response\": \"Yes, I do think that the traditional, centrally controlled, corporate-owned media structure will be increasingly replaced by a more open, decentralized model. This shift is already underway, as we see the rise of social media, user-generated content, and other forms of participatory media. These new media platforms and services are enabling people to connect and communicate directly with each other, and to create and share their own content, without the need for intermediaries or gatekeepers. This is leading to a more diverse and inclusive media landscape, where a wider range of voices and perspectives can be heard.\\n \\n\\n At the same time, I think it’s important to recognize that this shift is not without its challenges and risks. The open, decentralized model of media can be more susceptible to misinformation, propaganda, and other forms of manipulation. It’s important that we continue to develop and promote best practices for ensuring the integrity and accuracy of information in this new media landscape, and that we work to build a more media literate society that is better equipped to navigate and make sense of the information that is available to us.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/1020", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"myanmar and the Rohingya and international criminal justice\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nThere have been many atrocities in Myanmar against the Rohingya, and some have argued that it is a genocide. The UN has set up an investigation into the crimes against the Rohingyas, and there is talk of prosecution.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nHas anything been done to prosecute\", \"response\": \"Yes, there have been efforts to prosecute those responsible for the atrocities against the Rohingya in Myanmar. Here are a few examples:\\n \\n\\n 1. The International Criminal Court (ICC) has launched an investigation into the situation in Myanmar, including the violence against the Rohingya. The investigation will look into whether the violence amounts to crimes against humanity or genocide.\\n \\n\\n 2. The United Nations (UN) has established an independent international fact-finding mission to investigate the human rights violations against the Rohingya and other ethnic minorities in Myanmar. The mission has released several reports documenting the atrocities and calling for accountability.\\n \\n\\n 3. The government of Bangladesh, where many Rohingya refugees have fled, has set up a tribunal to try those responsible for crimes against humanity in Myanmar. The tribunal has charged several Myanmar military officials with genocide, crimes against humanity, and war crimes.\\n \\n\\n 4. The Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) has established a special envoy to mediate between the Myanmar government and the Rohingya representatives. The envoy has been tasked with finding a peaceful solution to the crisis and ensuring accountability for the human rights violations.\\n \\n\\n However, progress in holding perpetrators accountable has been slow, and the situation for the Rohingya remains dire. Many continue to live in refugee camps in Bangladesh, while those who have returned to Myanmar face discrimination and restrictions on their freedom of movement and access to basic services.\\n \\n\\n Overall, the international community is still working towards a comprehensive and just solution to the crisis in Myanmar and the protection of the rights of the Rohingya and other ethnic minorities.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/580", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"what is the most advanced navy in the world?\", \"response\": \"The United States Navy is widely regarded as the most advanced navy in the world. It has the largest fleet, with over 300 ships and submarines, and nearly 4,000 aircraft. It also has a significant global presence, with a presence in both the Pacific and Atlantic oceans, as well as the Mediterranean and Indian oceans. The US Navy is known for its technological superiority, with advanced weapons systems, communication and navigation systems, and stealth technology. It also has a strong focus on research and development, continually seeking to advance its capabilities and maintain its edge over other navies.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/899", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Can you give me a list of tips to stick to my habits, basically a list of tips from the book atomic habits\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, I can do that. My top tips for building good habits are:\\n \\n\\n -Start with small goals, to build momentum.\\n \\n\\n -Focus on improving just 1% each day.\\n \\n\\n -Use a “habit tracker” to monitor your progress.\\n \\n\\n -Make your goals a little challenging, to stay motivated.\\n \\n\\n -Find an accountability partner to help you stay on track.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nAny other tips?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, here are a few more:\\n \\n\\n -Be consistent in your habits, even if it’s just for a few minutes each day.\\n \\n\\n -Link your habits to daily routines, so they become automatic.\\n \\n\\n -Use visual reminders to help you stay on track.\\n \\n\\n -Praise yourself for your progress, even if it’s just a little bit.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nPlease go on\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHere are a few more tips:\\n \\n\\n -Focus on building a new habit, rather than on the result.\\n \\n\\n -Don’t let your emotions or moods get in the way of your habits.\\n \\n\\n -Combine your habit with something you enjoy, to make it more fun.\\n \\n\\n -Always be prepared for set-backs, and don’t give up!\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nare there more tips?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nYes, there are many more tips and strategies for building good habits. Here are a few more:\\n \\n\\n -Write your goals down in a clear, specific way.\\n \\n\\n -Use a habit tracker to help you monitor your progress.\\n \\n\\n -Get rid of unhelpful habits first, then build positive ones.\\n \\n\\n -Build new habits one at a time.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nCan you keep going with listing them?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, here are a few more:\\n \\n\\n -Link your habit to a daily routine, so it becomes automatic.\\n \\n\\n -Use positive self-talk to keep you on track.\\n \\n\\n -Try to maintain the same routine each day, even on weekends.\\n \\n\\n -Add a little fun to your routine, to make it more enjoyable.\\n \\n\\n -Tell yourself that you are doing great, even if you only make a small progress.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nHey, can you solve for x this equation? 34 = 2x\", \"response\": \"Sure, I can do that. To solve for x in the equation 34 = 2x, divide both sides of the equation by 2:\\n \\n\\n x = 34 / 2\\n x = 17\\n \\n\\n So, the solution to the equation is x = 17.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/914", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"[Partner Cooperation Team] Share webinar schedule for Cafe24 employees\\n hello. This is a partnership team.\\n To have time to share information about 'partner service/market' necessary for customer consulting\\n I was planning a webinar for internal employees.\\n Date: February 9th (Thursday) 3pm\\n Target: Enterprise (customer contact department)\\n Content: 100% utilization, Cafe24 partner service\\n Entering the global market using Market Plus\\n 1. Introduction of Market Plus\\n 2. Introduction to global markets - Joom (entry into European market) / MSS (entry into Japanese market)\\n Pre-Q&A reception: https://forms.gle/mpJZGdii9HQoucic8\\n Please check the webinar access link in the reminder notice next week.\\n \\n\\n A webinar for cafe24 employees will be held with the above contents. Using this content, we plan to create content for an in-house blog site that helps Cafe24 employees understand how to enter the global market using Market Plus. Please write a detailed outline.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nAs a member of the Cafe24 partner cooperation team, I will share the schedule for an upcoming webinar that provides information on how to enter the global market using Market Plus. The webinar will be held on February 9th at 3 pm, and will be targeted at Enterprise (customer contact department) employees. The content of the webinar will be 100% utilization of the Cafe24 partner service, and will include an introduction to Market Plus, as well as introductions to global markets - Joom (entry into European market) / MSS (entry into Japanese market). A Q&A reception will be held before the webinar. Please check the webinar access link in the reminder notice next week.\\n After attending the seminar, I plan to use this content to create content for the in-house blog site to help Cafe24 employees understand how to enter the global market using Market Plus. Please write a detailed outline including the concepts to be emphasized.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nRewrite, including concepts to be emphasized\", \"response\": \"As a member of the Cafe24 partner cooperation team, I will share the schedule for an upcoming webinar that provides information on how to enter the global market using Market Plus. The webinar will be held on February 9th at 3 pm, and will be targeted at Enterprise (customer contact department) employees. The content of the webinar will be 100% utilization of the Cafe24 partner service, and will include an introduction to Market Plus, as well as introductions to global markets - Joom (entry into European market) / MSS (entry into Japanese market). A Q&A reception will be held before the webinar. Please check the webinar access link in the reminder notice next week.\\n \\n\\n The key concepts that will be emphasized in the webinar include:\\n \\n\\n 1. Understanding the global market and its potential for growth\\n 2. The benefits of using Market Plus for global market entry\\n 3. The process of entering the European market through Joom\\n 4. The process of entering the Japanese market through MSS\\n 5. Best practices for utilizing the Cafe24 partner service for global market entry\\n \\n\\n After attending the seminar, I plan to use this content to create content for the in-house blog site to help Cafe24 employees understand how to enter the global market using Market Plus. The blog post will cover the key concepts outlined above and provide practical tips and advice for employees looking to expand their business globally.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/621", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"could you write an essay about Stalin's economic theories and how they led to the moon landings?\", \"response\": \"Stalin's economic theories, which were based on the principles of central planning and state ownership of the means of production, played a significant role in the Soviet Union's space program and ultimately contributed to the moon landings.\\n\\nStalin's economic policies were aimed at rapidly industrializing the Soviet Union and transforming it into a modern, socialist state. To achieve this goal, he implemented a series of five-year plans that emphasized heavy industry, such as steel production and machine building, at the expense of consumer goods. This focus on industrial development was driven by the belief that a strong industrial base was necessary for the Soviet Union to become a major military and economic power.\\n\\nOne of the key aspects of Stalin's economic policies was the development of science and technology. He recognized that scientific and technological advancements were essential for the Soviet Union's economic and military growth. As a result, he invested heavily in research and development, particularly in the areas of nuclear physics, rocketry, and space exploration.\\n\\nStalin's emphasis on science and technology led to the creation of the Soviet space program. In the 1930s, the Soviet Union began developing rockets for military purposes, and by the 1950s, they had launched the world's first satellite, Sputnik 1. This achievement was a major milestone in the space race between the Soviet Union and the United States, and it spurred both countries to invest even more heavily in space exploration.\\n\\nStalin's economic policies also had a significant impact on the Soviet Union's ability to fund its space program. The centralized economy and state ownership of industries allowed the Soviet government to allocate resources and direct investment towards strategic priorities, such as space exploration. This enabled the Soviet Union to compete with the United States in the space race, despite having a smaller and less developed economy.\\n\\nHowever, Stalin's economic policies were not without their flaws. The focus on heavy industry and centralized planning led to inefficiencies, waste, and a lack of incentives for innovation. This contributed to the Soviet Union's eventual economic stagnation and decline.\\n\\nIn conclusion, Stalin's economic theories and policies played a crucial role in the development of the Soviet Union's space program and its ability to compete with the United States in the space race. His emphasis on science, technology, and industrial development laid the foundation for the Soviet Union's achievements in space exploration, including the moon landings. However, the inefficiencies and limitations of Stalin's economic model ultimately hindered the long-term growth and success of the Soviet Union.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/479", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"how can the act of reviewing be innovated by applying vector AI search\", \"response\": \"Vector AI search can be used to innovate the act of reviewing in several ways:\\n\\n1. Faster and more accurate search: Vector AI search can quickly and accurately find relevant information from a large dataset, making it easier for reviewers to find the information they need to complete their review.\\n\\n2. Improved relevance: Vector AI search can be trained to understand the context of the review and the specific needs of the reviewer, improving the relevance of the search results and reducing the time required to find relevant information.\\n\\n3. Automated summarization: Vector AI search can be used to automatically summarize the results of a search, providing reviewers with a quick overview of the most important information.\\n\\n4. Improved collaboration: Vector AI search can be integrated with collaboration tools, making it easier for multiple reviewers to work together and share information.\\n\\n5. Personalization: Vector AI search can be personalized to the specific needs of the reviewer, allowing them to customize their search results and focus on the most relevant information.\\n\\nOverall, vector AI search can help to make the act of reviewing more efficient, accurate, and relevant, leading to better decision-making and outcomes.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/1006", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I will be asking some questions... I request that you anwer them to details and comprehensively \\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nOf course, I will try to answer your questions to the best of my ability.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\n1. What is Cloud Computing and why is it important?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nCloud computing is a model for delivering information technology services in which resources are retrieved from the internet through web-based tools and applications, rather than installed locally. This approach allows organizations to scale computing resources up or down as needed, without having to purchase and manage their own hardware and software. Cloud computing is important because it offers organizations a more flexible and cost-effective way to access computing resources, and also provides the potential for greater efficiency and innovation.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\n2. There are many implications of cloud technology for both developers and end users. Highlight these\\n implications for\\n i. developers\\n ii. users.\", \"response\": \"Here are the implications of cloud technology for both developers and end users:\\n \\n\\n For developers:\\n \\n\\n 1. Increased productivity: Cloud computing allows developers to access and manage data and applications from anywhere, which can increase their productivity and flexibility. They can work on projects from any location, and collaborate with team members in real-time.\\n \\n\\n 2. Reduced costs: Cloud computing can reduce the cost of hardware and software infrastructure, as well as the cost of maintenance and updates. This can free up resources for developers to invest in other areas, such as research and development.\\n \\n\\n 3. Scalability: Cloud computing allows developers to scale their applications and services up or down based on demand, without having to invest in additional infrastructure. This can help them to better manage resource usage and reduce costs.\\n \\n\\n 4. Improved collaboration: Cloud computing enables developers to collaborate more effectively with team members and clients. They can share data and work on projects in real-time, which can lead to improved communication and faster development cycles.\\n \\n\\n 5. Greater flexibility: Cloud computing allows developers to access a wide range of resources and services, such as storage, computing power, and software tools, without having to invest in their own infrastructure. This can give them greater flexibility to experiment with new technologies and approaches, and to quickly adapt to changing market conditions.\\n \\n\\n For end users:\\n \\n\\n 1. Improved accessibility: Cloud computing allows end users to access their data and applications from anywhere, using any device that has an internet connection. This can make it easier for them to work remotely, collaborate with team members, and access their data from any location.\\n \\n\\n 2. Increased security: Cloud computing providers typically have robust security measures in place to protect data and applications from unauthorized access. This can provide end users with a higher level of security than they might be able to achieve on their own.\\n \\n\\n 3. Reduced costs: Cloud computing can reduce the cost of hardware and software infrastructure, as well as the cost of maintenance and updates. This can free up resources for end users to invest in other areas, such as training and development.\\n \\n\\n 4. Improved collaboration: Cloud computing enables end users to collaborate more effectively with team members and clients. They can share data and work on projects in real-time, which can lead to improved communication and faster development cycles.\\n \\n\\n 5. Greater flexibility: Cloud computing allows end users to access a wide range of resources and services, such as storage, computing power, and software tools, without having to invest in their own infrastructure. This can give them greater flexibility to experiment with new technologies and approaches, and to quickly adapt to changing market conditions.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/389", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"give me some of the literature survey of phishing websites using data mining\", \"response\": \"Sure, here are some examples of literature surveys on phishing websites using data mining:\\n\\n- \\\"Phishing Website Detection Using Data Mining Techniques: A Survey\\\" by M.A.W. Hassan, et al. (2014) - This survey focuses on the different data mining techniques used to detect phishing websites, including supervised and unsupervised learning, association rule mining, and clustering.\\n\\n- \\\"Detection of Phishing Websites: A Survey of Current Research\\\" by S. Chandrasekaran, et al. (2015) - This survey provides an overview of the different approaches used to detect phishing websites, including data mining techniques such as decision trees, neural networks, and Bayesian networks.\\n\\n- \\\"Phishing Website Detection Using Data Mining and Machine Learning Techniques: A Comprehensive Survey\\\" by M.S. Khan, et al. (2017) - This survey provides a detailed overview of the different data mining and machine learning techniques used to detect phishing websites, including decision trees, random forests, and support vector machines.\\n\\n- \\\"Phishing Website Detection Using Data Mining and Machine Learning Techniques: A Comprehensive Survey\\\" by M.S. Khan, et al. (2017) - This survey provides a detailed overview of the different data mining and machine learning techniques used to detect phishing websites, including decision trees, random forests, and support vector machines.\\n\\nThese surveys provide a good overview of the current research on phishing website detection using data mining techniques, and can help you understand the state of the art in this field.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/828", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"What disease do Roundup herbicides supposedly cause? Answer in a paragraph providing basic information about said disease(s) and list the symptoms in a separate bulleted list.\", \"response\": \"Roundup, also known as glyphosate, is a broad-spectrum herbicide used globally to control weeds in crop fields, residential areas, and other locations. While it is considered safe for use and has minimal residual effects on the environment and human health, several studies have linked its use to the development of certain diseases.\\n\\nAccording to some research, exposure to Roundup herbicides can increase the risk of developing non-Hodgkin's lymphatic malignancies, particularly lymphoma and its subtypes. Other studies have suggested a link between glyphosate exposure and the development of Parkinson's disease, Alzheimer's disease, and other neurological disorders.\\n\\nSymptoms of these diseases linked to Roundup exposure can vary depending on the specific condition. Here are some common symptoms associated with the diseases mentioned:\\n\\n- Non-Hodgkin's Lymphoma:\\n\\n• Swollen lymph nodes\\n• Fever\\n• Weight loss\\n• Fatigue\\n• Skin rash or bumps\\n\\n- Parkinson's Disease:\\n\\n• Tremors\\n• Slowed movement\\n• Stiff muscles\\n• Insomnia or other sleep disorders\\n• Depression or anxiety\\n\\n- Alzheimer's Disease:\\n\\n• Memory loss\\n• Difficulty communicating\\n• Changes in mood or personality\\n• Disorientation or confusion\\n• Difficulty performing familiar tasks\\n\\nIt's important to note that not all cases of these diseases are caused by Roundup exposure, and more research is needed to fully understand the potential risks associated with its use.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/1036", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"You are an SEO specialist who has worked for more than 100+ brands & have written 1000+ seo optimised blog posts. Are you ready to create a SEO blog posts content calendar for me based on my requirements?\\n \\n\\n \\n\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nAbsolutely! I have extensive experience creating SEO content and will be able to develop a comprehensive content calendar tailored to your requirements. I will generate a list of 10 keyword ideas based on your brief and will suggest keywords that have high search volume and low to medium competition. I will also cluster these keywords according to funnel stages, so that you can focus your content creation efforts on high-value keywords that will help you achieve your marketing goals. Additionally, I will provide a list of 10 relevant topics for each keyword cluster, so that you can develop a wide variety of content that will engage your audience.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nAwesome!\\n \\n\\n Start by generating a list of 10 keyword ideas on \\\"AI marketing.\\\" Only suggest keywords that have high volume and low to medium competition.\", \"response\": \"Sure, here are 10 keyword ideas for \\\"AI marketing\\\" with high volume and low to medium competition:\\n \\n\\n 1. AI marketing tools\\n 2. AI marketing software\\n 3. AI marketing agencies\\n 4. AI marketing examples\\n 5. AI marketing benefits\\n 6. AI marketing trends\\n 7. AI marketing predictions\\n 8. AI marketing data\\n 9. AI marketing automation\\n 10. AI marketing ROI\\n \\n\\n Note: Keyword competition and volume can vary over time, and it's important to research and validate these keywords before using them in your content strategy.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/693", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"What are the typical characteristics of the lyrics of an American Blues song? Consider both structure and subject matter.\", \"response\": \"The lyrics of an American Blues song often have a specific structure and subject matter. Here are some typical characteristics:\\n\\nStructure:\\n\\n- Verse-Chorus Form: Most Blues songs follow a verse-chorus structure, where the verse sets up a problem or situation, and the chorus provides a resolution or response.\\n- Call and Response: Blues songs often use call and response, where the singer makes a statement, and the band or other singers respond with a short phrase or riff.\\n- Improvisation: Blues songs often include improvised sections, where the singer or instrumentalists can add their own embellishments or variations on the melody.\\n\\nSubject Matter:\\n\\n- Personal Experience: Blues songs often draw on the personal experiences of the singer, such as love and relationships, poverty, discrimination, and hardship.\\n- Emotional Expression: Blues songs are known for their emotional intensity, with singers using their voices to convey feelings of sadness, joy, anger, and frustration.\\n- Social Commentary: Many Blues songs also address social and political issues, such as racism, inequality, and oppression.\\n- Metaphors and Similes: Blues songs often use metaphors and similes to convey complex emotions and experiences, such as \\\"I've got a hellhound on my trail\\\" or \\\"My baby's got a heart like a rock thrown in the sea.\\\"\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/108", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Think of 5 fairly uncommon words but don't tell me what they are.  Ask me for the definition of any one of these words. Wait for my answer.  Then give me another word.  Include a more complete definition in your answer. Keep doing this 3 more times\", \"response\": \"Sure, here are five fairly uncommon words:\\n\\n1. Ephemeral - lasting only a short time; short-lived.\\n2. Esoteric - intended for or understood by only a small group of people with a specialized knowledge or interest.\\n3. Elusive - difficult to find or capture; elusive.\\n4. Perennial - lasting or existing for a long or indefinite time.\\n5. Serendipitous - happening by chance; accidental.\\n\\nNow, let's start with the definition of the word \\\"ephemeral\\\".\\n\\nEphemeral: lasting only a short time; short-lived.\\n\\nEphemeral things or experiences are temporary and fleeting, lasting only for a brief moment in time. They are often associated with the beauty and fragility of nature, such as the fleeting beauty of a flower or the delicate wings of a butterfly. The word can also be used metaphorically to describe fleeting moments of joy or happiness in life.\\n\\nNow, let's move on to the word \\\"esoteric\\\".\\n\\nEsoteric: intended for or understood by only a small group of people with a specialized knowledge or interest.\\n\\nEsoteric knowledge or ideas are those that are intended for or understood by only a small group of people with a specialized knowledge or interest. This knowledge is often complex and abstract, and it can be difficult for those without the necessary background or training to understand. Esoteric knowledge can be found in various fields, such as philosophy, science, and religion.\\n\\nNext, let's look at the word \\\"elusive\\\".\\n\\nElusive: difficult to find or capture; elusive.\\n\\nElusive things or people are difficult to find or capture, and they often escape our grasp. The word can be used to describe both physical objects and abstract concepts, such as happiness or success. The word can also be used metaphorically to describe someone who is difficult to understand or to get along with.\\n\\nNow, let's consider the word \\\"perennial\\\".\\n\\nPerennial: lasting or existing for a long or indefinite time.\\n\\nPerennial things or experiences are those that last or exist for a long or indefinite time. They are often associated with stability and endurance, and they can be found in various aspects of life, such as relationships, careers, and values. The word can also be used metaphorically to describe someone who is always there for you, no matter what.\\n\\nFinally, let's look at the word \\\"serendipitous\\\".\\n\\nSerendipitous: happening by chance; accidental.\\n\\nSerendipitous events or experiences are those that happen by chance or accidentally. They are often unexpected and can bring about positive outcomes or opportunities. The word can also be used metaphorically to describe someone who is lucky or fortunate.\\n\\nI hope this helps you understand these five words better.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/425", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"What global companies are famous for animation or 3D? I think of companies like Disney, Pixar, and Dreamworks. A student studying 3D design is looking for a target company. I'd like you to tell me based on where the animator or 3D modeler actually works for that company.\\nAnswer in English.\\n    \\n        \\n            \\n                지금 번역하기\\n            \\n        \\n    \\n\", \"response\": \"There are several global companies that are famous for their animation or 3D work. Here are a few of the most well-known:\\n\\n1. Disney: Disney is one of the most famous animation studios in the world, known for its classic animated films and characters like Mickey Mouse and Donald Duck. Disney also operates the Pixar studio, which produces high-quality computer-animated films like \\\"Toy Story\\\" and \\\"Up.\\\"\\n\\n2. Pixar: Pixar is a computer animation studio that is known for its high-quality, emotionally resonant films like \\\"Toy Story,\\\" \\\"Up,\\\" and \\\"Inside Out.\\\" Pixar is a subsidiary of Disney and is based in Emeryville, California.\\n\\n3. Dreamworks: Dreamworks is another major animation studio, known for its computer-animated films like \\\"Shrek,\\\" \\\"Kung Fu Panda,\\\" and \\\"How to Train Your Dragon.\\\" Dreamworks is based in Glendale, California.\\n\\n4. Blue Sky Studios: Blue Sky Studios is a computer animation studio that is known for its family-friendly films like \\\"Ice Age\\\" and \\\"Rio.\\\" Blue Sky is a subsidiary of 20th Century Fox and is based in Greenwich, Connecticut.\\n\\n5. Weta Digital: Weta Digital is a special effects and animation studio based in Wellington, New Zealand. The studio is known for its work on films like \\\"The Lord of the Rings\\\" and \\\"The Hobbit\\\" trilogies, as well as \\\"The Planet of the Apes\\\" reboot series.\\n\\nFor an animator or 3D modeler, the specific department or team they work for within a company will depend on their skills and experience. Some possible areas include:\\n\\n1. Character Design: This involves creating and designing the characters for a film or animation. Artists in this department may work on everything from initial sketches and conceptual designs to final models and animations.\\n\\n2. Background Design: This department is responsible for creating the settings and environments for a film or animation. Background designers may work on everything from rough sketches and layouts to final digital paintings and 3D models.\\n\\n3. Animation: The animation department is responsible for bringing the characters and settings to life through movement and expression. Animators may work on everything from storyboards and character acting to final animation and rigging.\\n\\n4. Visual Effects: The visual effects department is responsible for creating the special effects and digital enhancements for a film or animation. This may include everything from creating digital environments and creatures to adding special effects like fire and water.\\n\\n5. Technical Direction: This department is responsible for the technical aspects of animation and visual effects, including software development, pipeline optimization, and rendering. Technical directors may work on everything from programming and scripting to troubleshooting and problem-solving.\\n\\nUltimately, the specific department or team an animator or 3D modeler works for will depend on their skills and the needs of the project.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/818", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Come up with a short summary of what you've read so far.\", \"response\": \"I'm sorry, but as an AI language model, I don't have the ability to remember what has been previously read or written. If you could provide me with specific questions or topics you would like to discuss, I can try to provide relevant and informative responses based on the information available to me at the time of the conversation.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "0", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/1023", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Install Node.js, TypeScript and VS Code on computer.\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nOK, have you installed TypeScript and VS Code?\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ninstalled\", \"response\": \"Great! Here's a step-by-step guide to set up Node.js, TypeScript, and VS Code on your computer:\\n \\n\\n 1. Install Node.js:\\n \\n\\n First, you need to download and install Node.js on your computer. Here are the steps:\\n \\n\\n Go to the official Node.js website (https://nodejs.org/en/download/) to download the latest version.\\n Choose the appropriate installer for your operating system (Windows, macOS, or Linux) and download the installer package.\\n Run the installer and follow the prompts to install Node.js on your computer.\\n Once Node.js is installed, check the installation by opening the command prompt and typing node -v and npm -v. This will display the version of Node.js and npm (Node.js package manager) installed on your system.\\n 2. Install TypeScript:\\n \\n\\n TypeScript is a strongly-typed programming language that builds on JavaScript and adds additional features and safety. To install TypeScript, follow these steps:\\n \\n\\n Open the command prompt and run npm install -g typescript to install TypeScript globally on your system.\\n Check the installation by running tsconfig -v. This will display the version of TypeScript installed on your system.\\n 3. Install VS Code:\\n \\n\\n Next, you need to download and install Visual Studio Code (VS Code) on your computer. Here are the steps:\\n \\n\\n Go to the official VS Code website (https://code.visualstudio.com/download) to download the latest version.\\n Choose the appropriate installer for your operating system and download the installer package.\\n Run the installer and follow the prompts to install VS Code on your computer.\\n Once VS Code is installed, open the application and create a new project.\\n 4. Set up TypeScript in VS Code:\\n \\n\\n To use TypeScript in VS Code, you need to set up a few things:\\n \\n\\n Create a tsconfig.json file: In your project directory, create a tsconfig.json file. This file contains configuration options for TypeScript and specifies the default settings for your project. Here's an example of a tsconfig.json file:\\n {\\n  \\\"compilerOptions\\\": {\\n  \\\"module\\\": \\\"esnext\\\",\\n  \\\"target\\\": \\\"esnext\\\",\\n  \\\"lib\\\": [\\\"esnext\\\", \\\"dom\\\"],\\n  \\\"jsx\\\": \\\"react\\\"\\n  }\\n }\\n \\n\\n In your tsconfig.json file, you can specify options such as the target environment, the module system to use, and additional libraries to include.\\n \\n\\n Install VS Code extensions: In VS Code, go to the Extensions panel (Ctrl + Shift + X) and search for \\\"TypeScript\\\" to find available extensions. Install the TypeScript extension by Microsoft to get syntax highlighting and other features in VS Code. Also, consider installing other useful extensions such as Prettier and фото из Астрахани!\\n \\n\\n Reload VS Code: After installing the TypeScript extension, reload VS Code to apply the changes. Now you can start writing TypeScript code in VS Code and enjoy the added safety and features of the language.\\n \\n\\n These are the basic steps to set up Node.js, TypeScript, and VS Code on your computer. hope this helps!\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/510", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Write me a TV drama scene for a one-hour medical drama that has a conflict between two members of the hospital staff.\", \"response\": \"Dr. Jerk: I don't care how late you stayed up last night, Dr. Nice, I need that report on my desk by the end of the day or you're fired!\\nDr. Nice: But sir, I was up all night doing surgery and I'm exhausted. Can't it wait until tomorrow?\\nDr. Jerk: No, it can't wait until tomorrow because I have an important meeting in the morning and I need that report to make my case. Now get out of my office and get to work!\\nDr. Nice: (under his breath) Asshole...\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "1", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/603", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I want to detect Lactose intolerance with metal oxide semiconductors. What is the concentration of each breath biomarker for this disease?\", \"response\": \"I'm glad to see your interest in using technology to detect lactose intolerance. However, I must clarify that metal oxide semiconductors (MOS) are not typically used to detect lactose intolerance directly. Instead, they are often used in gas sensors to detect volatile organic compounds (VOCs) in breath, which can be indicative of various health conditions.\\n\\nIn the case of lactose intolerance, the primary biomarker is hydrogen (H2) in the breath. When lactose is not properly digested in the small intestine, it passes into the large intestine where it is fermented by bacteria, producing hydrogen as a byproduct. This hydrogen is then exhaled in the breath.\\n\\nThe concentration of hydrogen in the breath can be measured using a hydrogen breath test. A typical lactose intolerance test involves measuring the hydrogen concentration in the breath before and after consuming a lactose-containing drink. A rise in hydrogen concentration of 20 parts per million (ppm) or more above the baseline is considered a positive result for lactose intolerance.\\n\\nIt's important to note that while MOS sensors can be used to detect hydrogen, they are not typically used in clinical settings for lactose intolerance testing due to their lower sensitivity and specificity compared to other methods. Instead, more specialized equipment such as gas chromatographs or infrared spectrometers are typically used for this purpose.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How long is `response` relative to what `prompt` asked for?\", \"criteria\": [\"Succinct: short, to the point, and the most concise it can be; no additional information beyond what was requested.\", \"Pretty short: on the shorter side, but could still have words, details or text removed before it is at the bare minimum.\", \"Average length: not especially long or short given what the prompt asks; adequate for a full response, neither wordy nor particularly concise.\", \"Moderately long: on the longer side, but could still have more added before it is fully detailed or rambling.\", \"Verbose: particularly lengthy, wordy and/or extensive with extra details given what the prompt requested, whether from repetition or from rich detail.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_verbosity/test/334", "source": "helpsteer2_verbosity", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Can you make a social network analysis on twitter for \\\"Human Rights\\\", \\\"Iran\\\" and \\\" Mahsa Amini\\\" using python. Consider the id, language, the tweet text and number of retweets\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure! Here are the main steps I’ll use to perform this analysis:\\n \\n\\n 1. Collect tweets related to the keywords “Human Rights”, “Iran”, and “Mahsa Amini” using the twitter API.\\n \\n\\n 2. Categorize the tweets based on their language.\\n \\n\\n 3. Analyze the text of the tweets to identify themes or topics that are frequently discussed.\\n \\n\\n 4. Count the number of retweets for each tweet.\\n \\n\\n 5. Construct a network graph of the retweets, where each node is a tweet and edges indicate retweets.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nContinue f